<title>FRANCE: Danone 1997 Q1 sales up three pct.</title>
<headline>Danone 1997 Q1 sales up three pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover					20,103    vs   19,523</p>
<p>- breakdown for western Europe</p>
<p>	- dairy products			   5,422    vs    5,661</p>
<p>	- grocery products and pasta	   3,820    vs    4,019</p>
<p>	- biscuits				   2,740    vs    2,802</p>
<p>	- beverages				  2,881    vs    3,044</p>
<p>	- containers				 1,401    vs    1,550</p>
<p>    - International				4,418    vs    3,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Groupe Danone gave the results in a statement.</p>
<p>The year-over-year rise of 600 million francs includes the consolidation of new companies in Argentina and China representing around 400 million francs, currency shifts with a positive impact of around 400 million francs, and a drop in like-for-like sales of around 200 million francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
